@startuml sd_us213
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
title US213 - Sequence Diagram
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 260
actor "ATCC" as Actor
participant "Entry (Envoy)\nvirtual IP of flight-ops" as EFO
box "flight-ops-n (the replica that answers)" #F7F7F7
participant "FlightController" as FlightController
participant "ViewScheduledFlightsByAircraftUseCase" as ViewScheduledFlightsByAircraftUseCase
database "own database" as DBFO
end box
collections "peer replicas\nflight-ops-m" as PFO
participant "aircraft-maintenance\n(through aircraft-maintenance-local)" as OAM
== GET /api/flights?aircraftId={registration} ==
Actor -> EFO : GET /api/flights?aircraftId={registration}\n(HTTPS, Authorization: Bearer JWT)
EFO -> FlightController : to a ready replica\n(another one if it fails)
FlightController -> ViewScheduledFlightsByAircraftUseCase : execute(...)
ViewScheduledFlightsByAircraftUseCase -> OAM : C1: GET /internal/aircrafts/{registration}\n(the actor's token)
OAM --> ViewScheduledFlightsByAircraftUseCase : 200 the aircraft: status, model, seats, range, fuel consumption
ViewScheduledFlightsByAircraftUseCase -> DBFO : own flights
ViewScheduledFlightsByAircraftUseCase -> PFO : GET /internal/replicas/flights\n(every peer in parallel)
PFO --> ViewScheduledFlightsByAircraftUseCase : their flights
ViewScheduledFlightsByAircraftUseCase -> ViewScheduledFlightsByAircraftUseCase : keep the latest change of each record,\nleave out deleted ones; filter, compute, sort, page
ViewScheduledFlightsByAircraftUseCase --> FlightController : result
FlightController --> Actor : 200 OK (X-Node-Id; X-Partial-Result if both holders of a record were unreachable)
@enduml
